---
/**
 * Cloudflare Web Analytics.
 *
 * Counts visits, pages and referrers. It answers "did anyone open the link,
 * and when", which is what GMZ asked for. It deliberately does not answer
 * "who": there are no cookies, no cross-site identifiers and no visitor
 * profiles, so nothing here can name a client or follow one around the web.
 *
 * Inert until PUBLIC_CF_ANALYTICS_TOKEN is set, so local development and any
 * preview build stay untracked and the numbers reflect real visitors rather
 * than our own builds. Set it in the host's environment variables, the same
 * way SITE_URL is set, and rebuild: environment variables are read at build
 * time, so saving one changes nothing until a new build runs.
 *
 * Two things worth knowing before trusting the numbers:
 *
 * 1. The veil is client-side, so the page is delivered and counted before
 *    anyone types the code. A visit therefore includes people who arrived and
 *    gave up at the veil. Cloudflare's free tier is pageviews only, with no
 *    custom events, so it cannot separate "opened the link" from "got in". If
 *    that distinction starts to matter, a tool with custom events is needed.
 *
 * 2. It is a script, so ad blockers and JavaScript-off visitors are missed.
 *    Expect a genuine undercount rather than a precise figure.
 */
const token = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CF_ANALYTICS_TOKEN;
---

{
  token && (
    <script
      is:inline
      defer
      src="https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js"
      data-cf-beacon={JSON.stringify({ token })}
    />
  )
}
